From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:27:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dxvk: PLAYPORT_DXVK_MEMORY=1 logs [dxvk-mem], live memory by
 kind, on [kk-mem]'s cadence

A Vulkan play's graphics memory was only KosmicKrisp's [kk-mem]
memory= figure: the device memory DXVK allocated, with nothing saying
what it backs. Fitting SANABI's Black Market scene switch into the 8 GB
phone's limit (PLA-803) needs to know which of it grows.

With PLAYPORT_DXVK_MEMORY=1 (the dev app sets it; the release app never
does), the allocator counts each buffer and image allocation it hands
out under one kind until it is freed: images as render targets (colour
or depth-stencil attachment usage), storage images (storage usage, no
attachment) or sampled textures (the rest); buffers in host-visible
memory as staging and upload, the others as buffers. An allocation
moves to the pending frees when nothing but GPU work that has not
completed holds it: the storage a discard or a relocation retires into
the command list, and the storage of a resource whose last reference
other than GPU work goes. The pending frees are a list in release
order, so the oldest one's wait is known. Imported memory and sparse
pages are not counted. The counters live in dxvk_memory_census.h, which
makes no Vulkan call.

The line comes as [kk-mem] does (mesa 0135): from the submission
thread, every 10 s, and at most once a second as soon as the counted
memory grew by 64 MiB since the last line (marked "| growing
live+N MiB"):

  [dxvk-mem] metal=M allocated=A used=U | rt=n/MiB sampled=n/MiB
  storage=n/MiB staging=n/MiB buffers=n/MiB pending=n/MiB oldest=S s
  | cached=C free=F MiB

metal= is the driver's heap usage (VK_EXT_memory_budget: on
KosmicKrisp Metal's current allocated size, [kk-mem]'s metal=),
allocated= and used= the allocator's device memory and what of it is
suballocated. allocated is the kinds + pending + cached (what the
allocator's caches hold) + free (chunk space not handed out), so DXVK's
memory plus KosmicKrisp's own allocations ([kk-mem] internal,
descriptor, query, command, command-pooled) reconciles with metal=
(tools/memreconcile.py).

Without the variable nothing is counted: a release builds no census,
and a resource's release reads one flag first.

Linear: PLA-808
Class: diagnostics
Evidence: tools/tests/test_dxvk_memory_census.py, tools/tests/test_memreconcile.py (host); the phone run with Hollow Knight is PLA-808's acceptance, not run here
Offered-upstream: no
